  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Gray's Brain documents the physiological and psychological effects of the fictitious Hidden Rebellious Gene (HRG) on the brain in case study 666. The accordion book reads in two directions: Part A shows the damage caused by the HRG to the frontal cortex in series of MRI scans of the artist's brain. Part B recounts the psychological symptomatology of the mutant gene as an illustrated chronicle of 666's radical rebellious behavior (RRB) from age sixteen to twenty-four."--Publisher web site.</subfield>
  </datafield>
